      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7z-7 & =5z-3 \\\\ -7z-7-5z+7 & =5z-3-5z+7 \\\\ -12z & =4 \\\\ z & =- \\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-7z-7=5z-3$ has the unique solution $z=- \\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-1 & =z-1 \\\\ z-1-z & =z-1-z \\\\ -1 & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $z.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3z-8 & =-3z-3 \\\\ -3z-8+3z & =-3z-3+3z \\\\ -8 & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $z.$ Therefore, the equation $-3z-8=-3z-3$ has no solutions.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"",
