      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9w-5 & =9w+3 \\\\ 9w-5-9w & =9w+3-9w \\\\ -5 & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $w.$ Therefore, the equation $9w-5=9w+3$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7w+9 & =7w+9 \\\\ 7w+9-7w & =7w+9-7w \\\\ 9 & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $w.$\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7w-9 & =9w \\\\ -7w-9-9w+9 & =9w-9w+9 \\\\ -16w & =9 \\\\ w & =- \\frac{9}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-7w-9=9w$ has the unique solution $w=- \\frac{9}{16}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
