      ":question/problem": "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $3u+7=3u-9$\n- **II.** $6u-2=6u-8$\n- **III.** $-4u-6=5u+7$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3u+7 & =3u-9 \\\\ 3u+7-3u & =3u-9-3u \\\\ 7 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $3u+7=3u-9$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6u-2 & =6u-8 \\\\ 6u-2-6u & =6u-8-6u \\\\ -2 & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $u.$ Therefore, the equation $6u-2=6u-8$ has no solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4u-6 & =5u+7 \\\\ -4u-6-5u+6 & =5u+7-5u+6 \\\\ -9u & =13 \\\\ u & =- \\frac{13}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation $-4u-6=5u+7$ has the unique solution $u=- \\frac{13}{9}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
